diff --git a/.caliper/DECISIONS.md b/.caliper/DECISIONS.md
index dc5b385..3991b00 100644
--- a/.caliper/DECISIONS.md
+++ b/.caliper/DECISIONS.md
@@ -126,3 +126,9 @@ The project owner approved the full proposed architecture and first-slice scope
 - **Decision:** Use OpenCode's documented provider and authentication interfaces for provider discovery, supported API-key/OAuth methods, connection status, model discovery, and logout. Store the complete OpenCode authentication profile only as an encrypted Fernet Secret Store payload; PostgreSQL stores its secret reference and the selected provider/model identifier. OpenCode's working profile is materialized only in a memory-backed runtime directory and rehydrated from the encrypted payload at startup.
 - **Reason:** The owner selected a general OpenCode-based provider connection. OpenCode supports provider-specific API-key and OAuth methods, while D-018 prohibits plaintext credentials in operational storage.
 - **Consequences:** Never expose auth payloads or OAuth tokens in responses, logs, or errors. Use only provider IDs, methods, prompts, and models returned by the running OpenCode instance. If the encrypted profile cannot be restored, report provider authentication unavailable and do not fabricate a connected state.
+
+## D-021 — Per-project model assignment
+- **Status:** Accepted
+- **Decision:** Each project may select one model from the currently connected OpenCode providers or the latest successfully discovered Ollama catalog. Persist the provider kind, provider identifier, model identifier, and update time against that project in PostgreSQL. Changing a global provider connection does not silently rewrite project assignments; unavailable assignments remain visible and must be reselected from a fresh catalog.
+- **Reason:** The owner requested selecting a model for each project; the prior provider screens configured only a factory-wide default and did not satisfy project ownership.
+- **Consequences:** Assignment is configuration only. Model inference and execution remain outside this slice. API writes must validate against the current connected/discovered catalog and confirm the durable selection with a fresh read.
